# ============================================================================
# SSH Drive: folders on your servers as drives on this computer, or in your
# phone's Files app.
#
#   Windows   a drive letter (WinFsp when it's installed, Windows' own WebDAV
#             client when it isn't). Linux and macOS: a folder (sshfs).
#   Android   each drive appears in the Files app and in every app's "open".
#
#   Sign in with a password, a key or the SSH agent. The server's own key is
#   remembered the first time and a changed one is refused, as ssh does.
#   Lives in the tray, mounts its drives by itself and can start with the
#   computer. Everything is kept on this device only.
# ============================================================================

@Window SshDrive
Title=SSH Drive
Version=1.0
Width=480
Height=640
OnOpened=Start

